<BaseLayout title="School Life | Sarh Al Elm Private School" lang="en" description="Discover the learning environment and student experience at Sarh Al Elm Private School in Muscat."><section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><p>Beyond the classroom</p><h1>A school experience built around learning, belonging and growth</h1><span>At Sarh Al Elm, school life is about helping children develop academically while growing in confidence, curiosity and responsibility.</span></div></section><section class="intro wrap"><div><p class="kicker">The student experience</p><h2>Learning happens throughout the school day</h2></div><p>Our aim is to create an environment where students feel safe, supported and ready to participate. Classroom learning is complemented by opportunities to communicate, collaborate, explore interests and celebrate progress.</p></section><section class="cards wrap"><article><b>01</b><h3>Learning & discovery</h3><p>Students are encouraged to ask questions, practise essential skills and take an active role in their learning.</p></article><article><b>02</b><h3>Language & communication</h3><p>A bilingual learning environment supports communication, understanding and connection across the school community.</p></article><article><b>03</b><h3>Belonging & wellbeing</h3><p>We value a respectful school culture where children can feel known, supported and part of the community.</p></article><article><b>04</b><h3>Activities & participation</h3><p>School activities give students opportunities to participate, work with others and develop interests beyond routine lessons.</p></article></section><section class="gallery-cta"><div class="wrap"><div><p class="kicker">See the school in action</p><h2>Explore moments from Sarh Al Elm</h2></div><a href="/gallery/">Visit the school gallery →</a></div></section><section class="visit"><div class="wrap"><h2>Interested in joining our school community?</h2><p>Our admissions team can answer questions about Grades 1–8 and guide families through the enquiry process.</p><a class="btn-primary" href="/admissions/#enquiry">Start an admission enquiry</a></div></section></BaseLayout>
<style>
